/*  Bits — `0xFF`, `0b1010`, the arithmetic and the gates over them, `shifted left by`,
    `converted to hex`, `converted to number`, and a pattern written or set in a text.

    ★ A bits value is the runtime's `CufetBits` — its value, the base it is shown in and its width —
      passed by value. Everything it does is a runtime call `cufet build` makes too, so a result's
      base and width come out of one place for both compilers.

    ★ Two patterns compare on their VALUE alone: `0xFF`, `0x00FF` and `0b11111111` are one pattern
      written three ways, so a width is never what tells two apart.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// Whether an expression gives a bits value by what it is, whatever it is made from.
    Bind fact to is-bits-expression, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "BitsLiteral" or kind is "BitsShift" or kind is "BitsConvert" or kind is "BitsAtWidth".
    Done.

    /// A bits expression as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-bits-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "BitsLiteral":
            Define base as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)).
            Return "((CufetBits)\{ {(cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word}ULL, '{base}', {(cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word} \})".
        Done.
        Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "BitsShift":
            Define left as "0".
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word is "true", the left becomes "1".
            Define amount-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Return "cufet_bits_shift({target-c}, {amount-c}, {left}, {(cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word})".
        Done.
        If kind is "BitsConvert":
            Define base as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)).
            Return "cufet_bits_from_number({target-c}, '{base}', {(cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word})".
        Done.
        Define width-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Return "cufet_bits_at_width({target-c}, {width-c}, {(cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word})".
    Done.

    /// A binary operator over two bits values already as C: arithmetic and the gates give bits —
    /// the gates are calls, not `&&`, since combining two patterns needs both — and a comparison
    /// gives a fact, on the values alone.
    Bind text or failure to c-bits-binary, given (the text operator, the text left, the text right, the text at-line):
        Judge operator, where it is:
            "Plus", return "cufet_bits_add({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
            "Minus", return "cufet_bits_sub({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
            "Star", return "cufet_bits_mul({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
            "Slash", return "cufet_bits_div({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
            "Percent", return "cufet_bits_mod({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
            "And", return "cufet_bits_and({left}, {right})".
            "Or", return "cufet_bits_or({left}, {right})".
            "Xor", return "cufet_bits_xor({left}, {right})".
            "Equal", return "(({left}).value == ({right}).value)".
            "NotEqual", return "(({left}).value != ({right}).value)".
            "Lt", return "(({left}).value < ({right}).value)".
            "Gt", return "(({left}).value > ({right}).value)".
            "Lte", return "(({left}).value <= ({right}).value)".
            "Gte", return "(({left}).value >= ({right}).value)".
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on bits")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// What a binary operator gives when its left side is bits: bits for arithmetic and the
    /// gates, a fact for a comparison.
    Bind text to bits-binary-kind, given (the text operator):
        If operator is "Plus" or operator is "Minus" or operator is "Star" or operator is "Slash" or operator is "Percent"
                or operator is "And" or operator is "Or" or operator is "Xor":
            Return "bits".
        Done.
        Return "fact".
    Done.

    /// A bits value as the text it shows as — `0xFF`, prefix and all — in a buffer of its own.
    Bind text to c-bits-text, given (the text value):
        Return "(\{ char* cf_bt = (char*)cufet_arena_alloc(80); cufet_format_bits(cf_bt, 80, {value}); cf_bt; \})".
    Done.
Done.
